artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider a family of polynomials $\widetilde{W}_n(z^2;\kappa,\tau,\eta,\xi)$, indexed by $n\in\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$ and depending on parameters $\kappa,\tau,\eta,\xi$, that arises as a deformation of the Wilson polynomial family and satisfies a deformed three-term recursion relation (the modified Wilson polynomials, also referred to in the literature as Racah–Heun polynomials). For this family, determine the following analytic properties and, where possible, an explicit closed-form expression:

(a) a positive weight function (or measure) $w(z;\kappa,\tau,\eta,\xi)$ with respect to which the polynomials are orthogonal, together with the corresponding orthogonality relation;
(b) a generating function $\sum_{n\ge 0} \widetilde{W}_n(z^2;\kappa,\tau,\eta,\xi)\, t^n / c_n$ in closed form;
(c) the asymptotic behavior of $\widetilde{W}_n(z^2;\kappa,\tau,\eta,\xi)$ as $n\to\infty$ and as $z\to\infty$;
(d) a Rodrigues-type formula expressing $\widetilde{W}_n$ via repeated application of a differential or difference operator to a base function;
(e) explicit forward and backward shift operator relations linking $\widetilde{W}_n$ to $\widetilde{W}_{n\pm 1}$ with shifted parameters;
(f) the location and qualitative behavior of the zeros of $\widetilde{W}_n$;
(g) where possible, an explicit closed-form representation of $\widetilde{W}_n(z^2;\kappa,\tau,\eta,\xi)$ (for instance, in terms of (basic) hypergeometric series or known special functions).

